    "turn_text": "would agree with the first part and not the second. Are these things being brought into the fore which were typically held behind closed doors? Sometimes yes. And I think the reason why sometimes it has to be brought out into the public is because the true leverage points, the true push and pull that happens here in Washington Typically, there's always been by force of assignments from a speaker or a leader, force of fundraising by a speaker or a leader, or force by the web of interest groups that maneuver around Capitol Hill. So if you keep everything behind closed doors, then the people don't get to see the machinations of some of this stuff, and it takes away their ability to weigh it. Now, to the second piece about people trying to do that for personal game, I actually do disagree with that. And the reason why is a couple. Number one, if somebody gets popular, you know, myself, That's just a byproduct of people wanting to hear what I have to say and see me more and do that stuff. But I could tell you the vast majority of members, frankly, all the members, they're not doing this to try to build name IDs and so on and so forth. That comes as a byproduct of them communicating effectively or being a thought leader or being a fighter, quote unquote, or whatever the case might be. There are members on Capitol Hill. who everybody seems to know or there are members that nobody seems to know. That's all dependent on how each member decides to conduct themselves and handle their business. You brought them up, so I don't want to single them out. But with Dan Crenshaw, Dan does a lot of media. He chooses to do that. I do a lot of media. I choose to do that. That's just the way we go about our business. And so I think that it's not the right vein to say that the Freedom Caucus only does it because they want notoriety. The Freedom Caucus has these fights because they passionately care about the nation. And I would say the difference between Freedom Caucus members and probably other members of the Republican Conference is that we completely agree on strategy. We disagree on the tactical way to get there. It's a different difference in tactics. Oh,",
